Z||000000||Robert||11-18-2000||10:36 AM||||Since I leave my computer on all the time and I have a cable modem, I was wondering how easy it would be to host my own web page.  Is there software out there to do this?  What are the risks to my system?<BR>Thanks in advance.<P>Robert<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||alpha||11-18-2000||12:17 PM||||It is really easy. Just go to tucows and download a server daemon. From there you should get a domain name. Then you are in business.<P>Hosting a server is probably against your ISP's terms of service however.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-18-2000||02:32 PM||||I highly advise you NOT to do this....<P>there is a very large risk that your system would be hacked, through the web server. If you want to set up a web server in your home, get an older computer to use as the server (run linux on it), and set up a small LAN. Run your connection through the server, and use a software firewall like ZoneAlarm on your primary workstation.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
